{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999587-arcane-resistance","id":999587,"title":"Arcane Resistance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-06T23:12:36-08:00","id":999587,"title":"Arcane Resistance","content":"So, hello folks. How do you deal with the Merit Arcane Resistance in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T23:43:32-08:00","id":999597,"title":"","content":"For mages forbidden because it is worded as being separated from magic.<br /> From all the versions published I like the scaleable best. Want to be resistant to Thaumaturgy? Pay X. All forms of Blood Magic? Pay X+. Awakened Magick? Pay X++. Enlightened Science as well? Etc...<br /> <br /> Mechanically I deal with it as written.<br /> Increase difficulty by 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T00:26:17-08:00","id":999607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999587-arcane-resistance?p=999597#post999597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For mages forbidden because it is worded as being separated from magic.<br /> From all the versions published I like the scaleable best. Want to be resistant to Thaumaturgy? Pay X. All forms of Blood Magic? Pay X+. Awakened Magick? Pay X++. Enlightened Science as well? Etc...<br /> <br /> Mechanically I deal with it as written.<br /> Increase difficulty by 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see and I use the same, basically it should make little sense for a character to be resistant to ALL kinds of magic (I think the book states that by paying 5 points your resistance apply to every kind of magic), but then again that question that always arises: &quot;when should such resistance take place&quot; i.e. If I attempt to curse the magical resistant being, it's obvious that the resistance should take place, but what about an (in)famous fireball etc? Should the +2 Difficult apply to magical missiles, lighting bolts falling from the sky etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:12:00-08:00","id":999626,"title":"","content":"Yeah, given that Mage is all about Magick, it's pretty OP to have a flat resistance to all forms of Magick. At least with Vampires, threats that are magical in nature are tightly defined and limited to a specific educated minority (Vampiric blood sorcerers).<br /> <br /> Plus, we have Primium for a reason. And any Mage can attempt Countermagic or Anti-Magic, so long as they have at least one in the relevant Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:54:08-08:00","id":999638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999587-arcane-resistance?p=999626#post999626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, given that Mage is all about Magick, it's pretty OP to have a flat resistance to all forms of Magick. At least with Vampires, threats that are magical in nature are tightly defined and limited to a specific educated minority (Vampiric blood sorcerers).<br /> <br /> Plus, we have Primium for a reason. And any Mage can attempt Countermagic or Anti-Magic, so long as they have at least one in the relevant Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see and agree that to have a flat resistance to all forms of Magics or Magicks is very OP. I run a kind of cross over and there is a player with a reserve vampire char who has this merit (yes, as my chonicles tend to be deadly I usually advise my players to have a reserve char or two ready to play etc and I think it's always a good idea in long chronicles...) and I'm thinking in advance about ways to balance things out should he need to play with such character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:00:39-08:00","id":999656,"title":"","content":"If the bearer of the Arcane Resistance is not the target of the awakened will (as in case of the fireball) then you could give the bearer a bonus to soak it if you want to be nice. If the magick wirks completely indirect (destroy the bridge) the bearer is SOL.<br /> <br /> In a crossover with mage you could simply ban/change the merit.<br /> One possible change would be to give a countermagic dicepool independent of occult ability/magic knowledge.<br /> Another thing: there is a 15 point merit Immunity to Death in the Bygone Bestiary and the Guide to the Traditions. If they want complete immunity make them pay 15 freebies and give him flat out Immunity to Magic(k).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:25:35-08:00","id":1000012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999587-arcane-resistance?p=999656#post999656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the bearer of the Arcane Resistance is not the target of the awakened will (as in case of the fireball) then you could give the bearer a bonus to soak it if you want to be nice. If the magick wirks completely indirect (destroy the bridge) the bearer is SOL.<br /> <br /> In a crossover with mage you could simply ban/change the merit.<br /> One possible change would be to give a countermagic dicepool independent of occult ability/magic knowledge.<br /> Another thing: there is a 15 point merit Immunity to Death in the Bygone Bestiary and the Guide to the Traditions. If they want complete immunity make them pay 15 freebies and give him flat out Immunity to Magic(k).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much for the post. Well, I don't like much the idea of baning the merit, as it could look like I'm &quot;protecting the magical side of the story&quot; lol...in any case, I use the rules for night creatures to use wit+ occult (limited by WP) to resist direct effects etc. Letting him get complete immunity would change the game in a very deep and complex level, so I'd say this should not be an option.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:36:23-08:00","id":1000382,"title":"","content":"Concerning the Wits + Occult angle, I had an idea the other day about this. Assuming that's what we're going with, I would necessitate that the actual act of performing Countermagic for Night Folk is not Reflexive. It's not just this passive thing that instantly subtracts from the magick of Mages. You actually need to perform an action (that the character figures out using their knowledge of Occult matters) that is relevant to the Magick they're resisting. Kind of like how, when Mages have a certain rank in the Echoes Flaw, other characters can use the traditional banes of that Mage's Focus to get countermagic. It becomes a matter of the Night Folk needing to actively resist magick with their actions.<br /> <br /> For example, a Witch points a finger at a vampire and declares a hex on him. The vampire, in the act of countering it, spits on the ground and crosses himself. Or a werewolf comes under mind assault, and they imagine a brick wall, or start thinking a repetitive phrase over and over. Or a Sorcerer has just been tricked into drinking a magically poisoned drink, and they shove a finger down their throat to purge it. Stuff that resists the mythic threads that Mages use by pulling on Mythic Threads of their own. It gets the non-Mage characters more involved, and rewards them doing their research on their opponents (resisting a Fae-blooded Mage is a lot easier if you happen to have an iron nail in your pocket).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:48:36-08:00","id":1000388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999587-arcane-resistance?p=1000382#post1000382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the Wits + Occult angle, I had an idea the other day about this. Assuming that's what we're going with, I would necessitate that the actual act of performing Countermagic for Night Folk is not Reflexive. It's not just this passive thing that instantly subtracts from the magick of Mages. You actually need to perform an action (that the character figures out using their knowledge of Occult matters) that is relevant to the Magick they're resisting. Kind of like how, when Mages have a certain rank in the Echoes Flaw, other characters can use the traditional banes of that Mage's Focus to get countermagic. It becomes a matter of the Night Folk needing to actively resist magick with their actions.<br /> <br /> For example, a Witch points a finger at a vampire and declares a hex on him. The vampire, in the act of countering it, spits on the ground and crosses himself. Or a werewolf comes under mind assault, and they imagine a brick wall, or start thinking a repetitive phrase over and over. Or a Sorcerer has just been tricked into drinking a magically poisoned drink, and they shove a finger down their throat to purge it. Stuff that resists the mythic threads that Mages use by pulling on Mythic Threads of their own. It gets the non-Mage characters more involved, and rewards them doing their research on their opponents (resisting a Fae-blooded Mage is a lot easier if you happen to have an iron nail in your pocket).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very nice observations! I'm also not very found of the idea of the &quot;resist magick action&quot; being reflexive as it can seriously damper the power of the magi in a cross over chronicle, I quite liked your ideals concerning the act of resisance etc, besides it adds a lot of flavour to the game, something that's always helpful specially when we're talking about a dark ages game. Thank you very much sir.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}